I wanted an atheist extinctionist, which is really no harder than
extinctionist, and seemed to be a lazy man's way to some distinction other
than plain extinctionist.  I also wanted to try and collect the six neutral
quest artifacts, and managed to do so.

A faster extinctionist than this one (106K turns) is very possible.  I
fooled around for many turns doing these things:
 - polypiling ad nauseum - can't help it - I'm addicted to polymorphing
stuff.
 - making "MB and eating them until I acquired MB intrinsic
 - making +7 armor
 - making +9 silver daggers
 - making high-charge =IncDam and =GainConst
 - alchemizing and chugging potions when I really didn't need the extra HP
or Pw.
 - collecting dilithium crystals
 - waited for many turns for the demon princes to summon their brethren, but
gave up after a while.  I actually stoned them, hauled the statues to
Sokoban.  A few times during the course of the game I revived them and hoped
and waited for them to gate in another prince.
 - tamed 7 of the 9 Nazguls and saved them all up on Dlvl 1.  I wanted to
see how many I could ascend with, but only made it through the planes with
two.  not sure why count reflects as it does, hope I didn't miss any.

The castle wand of wishing was spent only for the artifacts wea116 was
carrying, and maybe one magic marker.  A few subsequent wishes from smoky
potions (!monster detection) were burned trying to get the Heart of Ahriman
(finally did), and then a couple more markers.

My strategy for speed extinctionist is simple:  create monsters as quickly
as possible with pets (Archons) killing them as fast as you make them.  I
hung out in Vlads Tower, casting CM, reading ?CM, zapping /CM until I
finally tamed an archon or two.  Then I started giving them good armor and
enchanting their weapons.  Once I had pet Archons I kept making monsters as
fast as I could and the Archons easily kill everything instantly, except
'trices.

